<title>UK: Nestle ups December 2001 bond to 500 million marks.</title>
<headline>Nestle ups December 2001 bond to 500 million marks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nestle Holding Inc has increased to 500 million marks from 400 million marks the size of the December 2001 Eurobond it launched earlier Thursday, lead manager SBC Warburg said.</p>
<p>The new paper has a 99.86 reoffer price. The deal will not be further increased.  </p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> AMT    500 MLN DEM   COUPON     5.125     MATURITY    21.DEC.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.44    PAY DATE    29.OCT.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    *	   SPREAD	+16 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.75	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  SWITZERLAND</p>
<p> NOTES     *INITIAL 400 MLN DEM REOFFERED AT 99.69</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
